<p>*Manifests in answer to PM request*</p>
<p>I have to echo Peppersghost here; this is a soup of concepts with way, way too much going on and nothing holding it together.</p>
<p>That said, I could maybe see the seed of an surreal-horror-comedy scip in &quot;a cow which is not a cow&quot; if you strip away all the cruft and just focus on the idea of something incredibly wrong that seems to want to be a cow for whatever reason- the narrative arc being something like a series of observation logs gradually ratcheting up the subtle creep factor. Never anything blatant, just enough that we get the idea that we probably want it to keep being a cow. Challenge factor would be extremely high, though- could easily go off the rails without rock-solid writing.</p>

